From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jinyu Meng <megabitsenmzq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Align linear output formats to 32 pixels

When decoding to untiled/linear output formats (NV12, NV21, YUV420,
YVU420), the Cedrus hardware still reconstructs and writes back macroblocks
in 32x32 tiles internally, and VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA requires
a 16-byte aligned half-width chroma stride (which means a 32-byte aligned
luma stride).

Currently, cedrus_prepare_format() and cedrus_dst_format_set() only align
width and height to 16 pixels for linear formats. When decoding streams
whose width is a multiple of 16 but not 32 (such as 720x1280, 720x576, or
720x480), the chroma stride is 360 bytes (not 16-byte aligned). This
corrupts the chroma plane written into the decoded picture buffer (DPB)
and causes severe green/purple chroma corruption across subsequent P/B
frames in both H.264 and HEVC decoding.

Align linear output width and height to 32 pixels so that both luma and
chroma strides satisfy the hardware alignment requirements, matching the
stride alignment already used for V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_32L32.

Fixes: 50e761516f2b ("media: platform: Add Cedrus VPU decoder driver")
Fixes: 193cd0fd5a60 ("media: cedrus: Add support for additional output formats")
Signed-off-by: Jinyu Meng <megabitsenmzq@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c    | 6 +++---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ void cedrus_dst_format_set(struct cedrus_dev *dev,
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YVU420:
-		chroma_size = ALIGN(width, 16) * ALIGN(height, 16) / 2;
+		chroma_size = ALIGN(width, 32) * ALIGN(height, 32) / 2;
 
 		switch (fmt->pixelformat) {
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
@@ -127,8 +127,8 @@ void cedrus_dst_format_set(struct cedrus_dev *dev,
 		reg = chroma_size / 2;
 		cedrus_write(dev, VE_PRIMARY_CHROMA_BUF_LEN, reg);
 
-		reg = VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_LUMA(ALIGN(width, 16)) |
-		      VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(ALIGN(width, 16) / 2);
+		reg = VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_LUMA(ALIGN(width, 32)) |
+		      VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(ALIGN(width, 32) / 2);
 		cedrus_write(dev, VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE, reg);
 
 		break;
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -181,11 +181,11 @@ void cedrus_prepare_format(struct v4l2_pix_format *pix_fmt)
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YVU420:
-		/* 16-aligned stride. */
-		bytesperline = ALIGN(width, 16);
+		/* 32-aligned stride. */
+		bytesperline = ALIGN(width, 32);
 
-		/* 16-aligned height. */
-		height = ALIGN(height, 16);
+		/* 32-aligned height. */
+		height = ALIGN(height, 32);
 
 		/* Luma plane size. */
 		sizeimage = bytesperline * height;
-- 
